<title>UK: Aluminium output fell in February -IPAI.</title>
<headline>Aluminium output fell in February -IPAI.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daily average primary aluminium output in February fell to 57,000 tonnes compared with 57,600 in January and 50,500 in February 1996, provisional figures from the International Primary Aluminium Institute (IPAI) show.</p>
<p>Total production in February (28 days) was 1.596 million tonnes, compared with 1.785 million in January (31 days) and 1.465 million in February 1996 (29 days).  </p>
<p>The regional breakdown of primary aluminium production was as follows (in thousands of tonnes) the IPAI said.</p>
<p>			 Feb'97   Jan'97    Feb'96</p>
<p>Africa		    84     93	  69</p>
<p>N.America		455    502	 464</p>
<p>S.America		163    178	 167</p>
<p>Asia		     267    318	 132</p>
<p>Europe West	    247    273	 253</p>
<p>Europe East/Central  251    278	 252</p>
<p>Oceania		  129    143	 128</p>
<p>--London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
